@copyright    Copyright (c) 2005-2025 The Regents of the University of California.
@license      http://opensource.org/licenses/MIT MIT

An item that names no component.

It is a page the template draws itself. The router still makes the item
active, so the page keeps its Itemid - and with it the modules assigned to
that page, its template style and its place in the menu - and only the
component area is left empty.

Its use is a hub whose front page is the template's own: set this item as the
default, and the template's home layout has the page to itself. Since there is
nothing for the menu to link to, it keeps out of the menu unless it is told
otherwise.
-->

<form>
	<fields name="params">
		<fieldset name="menu-options"
			label="COM_MENUS_LINKTYPE_OPTIONS_LABEL"
		>

			<field name="menu_show" type="radio"
				label="COM_MENUS_ITEM_FIELD_MENU_SHOW_LABEL"
				description="COM_MENUS_ITEM_FIELD_MENU_SHOW_DESC"
				default="0" filter="integer"
			>
				<option value="0">JNO</option>
				<option value="1">JYES</option>
			</field>

		</fieldset>
	</fields>
</form>
